QUANTIZATION RECIPE
    The `config_groups` and `ignore` list used by quant/glm53_quant_stream.py are
    taken VERBATIM from:

        QuantTrio/GLM-5.2-Int4-Int8Mix
        https://huggingface.co/QuantTrio/GLM-5.2-Int4-Int8Mix
        (config.json -> quantization_config)

    The recipe -- which layers are 4-bit vs 8-bit, group vs channel strategy, and
    critically WHICH MODULES ARE LEFT AT FULL PRECISION (MoE router, DSA indexer,
    LM head, layer 0, MTP norms) -- is theirs. This repository applies it to a
    different base model; it does not originate it.

BASE MODEL
    zai-org/GLM-5.3 and zai-org/GLM-5.3-BF16
    https://huggingface.co/zai-org/GLM-5.3-BF16
    Subject to the upstream model license (see the base model repository).

GB10 / sm121 SERVING RECIPE
    launch/launch-glm53-tp4.sh is derived from launch.sh in:

        tonyd2wild/GLM-5.2-QuantTrio-200K-4x-DGX-Spark--36tok-s
        https://github.com/tonyd2wild/GLM-5.2-QuantTrio-200K-4x-DGX-Spark--36tok-s

    which is itself derived from launch.sh in:

        CosmicRaisins/glm-5.2-gb10
        https://github.com/CosmicRaisins/glm-5.2-gb10
        Copyright (c) CosmicRaisins, licensed under the Apache License, Version 2.0.

    The 10 sm12x Triton sparse-MLA kernel overlays and the modded vLLM image
    required to run this on GB10 are NOT vendored here. Obtain them from the
    GLM-5.2-QuantTrio repository above, which vendors a known-good MATCHED set.
    Do not mix those overlays with a fresh upstream vLLM checkout: deepseek_v2.py
    imports `fused_indexer_q_rope_quant` from sparse_attn_indexer.py, and version
    skew between the two breaks model registration.

QUANTIZATION LIBRARY
    quant/glm53_quant_stream.py calls compressed-tensors' own calculate_qparams(),
    quantize() and pack_to_int32() rather than reimplementing scale computation or
    int4/int8 bit packing.

        https://github.com/neuralmagic/compressed-tensors
        Apache License, Version 2.0

    vLLM (Apache-2.0) -- https://github.com/vllm-project/vllm

